{
  "contract": "schema diff of two fp1 canonical documents, with the security relevance of each difference",
  "specification": "exponetdb-docs/03-database-model/schema-fingerprints.md#6-hierarchy-for-diffs; exponetdb-docs/03-database-model/drift-detection.md#7-wave-4-implementation-kind-c",
  "notes": "input.left and input.right name vectors of fp1.json. Entries match by class and key; equal entry hashes are matched (a different documentation digest only lists the entry in documentationChanged); otherwise the entry is changed and attributes lists, sorted, the top-level attribute names whose JCS forms differ. removed and changed follow the left document order, added the right document order (class, then key, UTF-8 byte order). comparable is false when the canonicalizer or the PostgreSQL major differ; the structure is still compared. securityRelevant follows drift-detection.md section 7: any difference of a policy, default privileges or event trigger; an added or removed SECURITY DEFINER function; a changed acl or owner of any object; changed row security flags of a table; a changed securityDefiner or config of a function. Expected values were derived by the same independent Python script as fp1.json.",
